  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Critical Support to Afghan Refugees and Migrants in Iran</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this project, IOM aims to support the Government of Iran with migration management support, including through the strengthening of border management infrastructure, and training of local institutions and border officers on protection issues affecting migrants, with a particular focus on counter-trafficking and counter-smuggling. In particular, IOM will aim to support the national Government to enhance access to durable solutions for vulnerable Afghans and their families while avoiding them having to resort to trafficking and smuggling networks. This includes the preparatory actions for the implementation of Humanitarian Corridors/Evacuations for their safe and dignified movement to and admission in Italy, the implementation of pre-migration health activities, as well as pre-departure orientation for parts of the caseload where the latter support is not provided by other actors. IOM will also support initiatives that ensure the inclusion of migrants and refugees in recovery processes, aiming to facilitate social cohesion and community stabilization, in a protection sensitive manner.</narrative>
  </description>
